# Aetherion — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
Aetherion (RetirementOS) — AI operating system for retirement and pension decisions in regulated financial institutions. Starting with Swedish occupational pension advisory workflows.

## Tech Stack
- **Backend:** Python 3.11+ / FastAPI
- **Frontend (prototype):** v0.dev (Vercel) — full Workbench UI prototyped here first
- **Frontend (production):** Next.js 14+ (App Router) / React / TypeScript — migrated from v0
- **Database:** PostgreSQL + pgvector
- **UI:** shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS (v0 uses these by default)
- **Auth:** WorkOS
- **LLM:** Anthropic Claude API
- **Doc generation:** python-docx, WeasyPrint, Jinja2
- **Infra:** Docker, Azure

## Frontend Strategy
The Workbench UI is being prototyped in v0.dev, then migrated into the repo. This means:
- Backend API design is the priority — make endpoints clean and well-documented so v0 can consume them
- When working on backend, always define clear Pydantic response schemas (these become the API contract for the frontend)
- The frontend/ directory will be populated when we migrate from v0
- For now, Cursor focus is on backend code, API endpoints, and database work

